# The export golden file is pinned byte for byte, CRLF line endings and UTF-8 BOM
# included (see tests/fixtures/export/README.md). `-text` stops git normalizing either on
# checkout or commit, which would fail the test on any machine configured with
# `core.autocrlf`.
#
# Deliberately *not* `binary`: that is a macro for `-diff -merge -text`, and killing the
# diff would defeat the point of a golden file, which is that you read the change before
# accepting it.
tests/fixtures/export/dives.csv -text

# The UDDF corpus is a captured download, and the point of keeping it is that it is byte
# for byte what the server sent. Nothing would notice git rewriting it: XML 1.0 normalizes
# literal CRLF to LF before the parser sees it, so a wholesale line-ending rewrite still
# validates against the XSD. Same `-text`, same reason for not saying `binary`.
tests/fixtures/uddf/demo-account.uddf -text
